Dissatisfied with other hosted MAC address OUI vendor lookup tools, I made my own.<p>Nothing but a search-as-you-type input.<p><a href="https:&#x2F;&#x2F;oui.so" rel="nofollow">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;oui.so</a><p>Also, it works really well with curl:<p><pre><code>  $ curl oui.so&#x2F;b4:b9:e6:28:f1:ab | jq
  [
    {
      &quot;oui&quot;: &quot;B4B9E6&quot;,
      &quot;name&quot;: &quot;eero inc.&quot;,
      &quot;address&quot;: &quot;660 3rd Street  San Francisco CA US 94107&quot;
    }
  ]</code></pre>

Wasm exports are immediately available to TypeScript, even gc objects!<p>```
&lt;script type=&quot;text&#x2F;wast&quot;&gt;
(module
  (type $Box (struct (field $val (mut i32))))
  (global $box (export &quot;box&quot;) (ref $Box) (struct.new $Box (i32.const 42)))
)
  &lt;&#x2F;script&gt;
&lt;script type=&quot;text&#x2F;typescript&quot;&gt;
const greeting: string = &quot;Hello from TypeScript and Wasm!&quot;;
console.log(greeting, box.val);
&lt;&#x2F;script&gt;
